* Bridges (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own script and our own art).
* Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder); the bridge
* objects are made anew each load and the room edits are safe to repeat.
*
* Upper east, airlock side: a catwalk across the gap between the platform
* west of it (room 156, floor y 1326) and the one east of it (room 182,
* floor y 1304). The gap is room 227, x 7720-7934, whose floor was an
* open door into room 177 below, so creatures walking east fell through.
* Sprite zcwk is drawn by art/catwalk.py (no railings; deck
* joins measured against both platforms), placed at x 7720, y 1240.

* the walkway: a floor line rising from the west platform's floor (room
* bottom, 0 up) to the east platform's (22 px up at the right wall), and
* the floor door below made as solid as the platforms' own floors. The gap's
* room allowed nothing to be dropped in it (drop status 0): now above its
* floor (1), as the platforms beside it, so the hand can put a creature down
* on the catwalk (owner, 2026-11-22).
room 227 7720 1175 7934 1326 room 227 4 room 227 5 room 227 6 room 227 7 room 227 8 room 227 9 room 227 12 room 227 13 room 227 14 room 227 15 room 227 16 room 227 17 1
ssfc 227 2 0 0 214 22
setv door 0 227 177 100

* the catwalk picture, behind creatures (plane 1500) and objects
enum 2 3 220 kill targ next
inst new: simp zcwk 1 0 600 0 setv cls2 2 3 220 setv attr 0 mvto 7720 1240 slow

* West, the Gelsemium pit: a sand ramp down into the glass observation
* tube under the walkway, whose west end looks out into the sea. The pit
* (room 202, x 1211-1334) used to drop creatures 145 px into the tube
* (room 189, x 840-1473), which had no other way in or out. Creatures only
* change rooms by walking out of a room's side, so the ramp gets a room of
* its own: 202 grows into one tall room, x 1211-1440, y 819-1140, whose
* floor follows the owner's sketched line: along the top of the tube's
* dune (y 1085 at the sea end to 1062 at x 1211), leaving it gently and
* steepening to the east walkway (y 964 at x 1440). The east walkway
* (201) now starts at x 1440, and the tube (189) keeps x 840-1211 with the
* sea end. The mushroom alcove (200) to the west is left as a ledge: a
* creature there can drop onto the ramp but cannot climb back.
* ROOM takes all the room's data, so each room's own values are passed back.
room 202 1211 819 1440 1140 room 202 4 0 room 202 6 room 202 7 room 202 8 room 202 9 room 202 12 room 202 13 room 202 14 room 202 15 room 202 16 room 202 17 room 202 19
ssfc 202 7 0 78 47 82 79 86 117 99 159 125 201 153 229 176
room 201 1440 819 1553 990 room 201 4 room 201 5 room 201 6 room 201 7 room 201 8 room 201 9 room 201 12 room 201 13 room 201 14 room 201 15 room 201 16 room 201 17 room 201 19
ssfc 201 2 0 26 113 22
room 189 840 990 1211 1140 room 189 4 room 189 5 room 189 6 room 189 7 room 189 8 room 189 9 room 189 12 room 189 13 room 189 14 room 189 15 room 189 16 room 189 17 room 189 19
ssfc 189 4 0 55 138 62 327 73 371 78
setv door 0 202 201 255
setv door 0 202 189 255

* the spring toy (2 13 1) that stood at the foot of the ramp goes: it
* bounced creatures up out of the tube and onto the alcove ledge. Only a
* spring in the ramp and tube area is removed, so others elsewhere stay.
enum 2 13 1 doif posl lt 1500 doif posr gt 1150 doif post lt 1125 doif posb gt 980 kill targ endi endi endi endi next

* the foreground overlay piece over the tube's east half (family 1, sprite
* fore, plane 8999, at x 1155, y 952, 384x224) draws the pit stones, the
* brass band and a dithered glass sheen in front of everything, so it
* covered the ramp (the sheen showed as a mesh on the sand). The
* background has the same stones and band, so only that piece goes.
enum 1 0 0 doif posl eq 1155 doif post eq 952 kill targ endi endi next

* the column east of the ramp: removing the overlay piece above also
* removed the front copy of the column's foot and base slab, so creatures
* walking behind the column showed their feet. Sprite zpln (our own, from
* art/plinth.py) puts a plinth back in front, at the overlay's
* plane.
enum 2 3 226 kill targ next
inst new: simp zpln 1 0 8999 0 setv cls2 2 3 226 setv attr 0 mvto 1448 953 slow

* the ramp's picture: sprite zsrp, drawn by art/sandramp.py (the
* tube's dune built up into a sand ramp, the opening above it, and the
* glass reflection west of it painted out so the tube's glass ends at the
* middle brass band), placed at x 1205, y 950, behind creatures
enum 2 3 225 kill targ next
inst new: simp zsrp 1 0 600 0 setv cls2 2 3 225 setv attr 0 mvto 1205 950 slow

* The pond by the incubator (owner, 2026-11-09): a creature that fell or was
* dropped in could not get out (the doorways from the water, room 19, to
* the bank, room 17, and to the lift's side were solid). Its right bank now
* slopes up out of the water along the background's own bank, which meets
* the water at about x 4630 and rises to the water pump's mound (y ~855 at
* x 4715). The pond's rooms (18 air, 19 water) end at x 4630 instead of
* 4680 and the bank (17) starts there. Room 19's floor runs flat at y 941 to
* x 4520, then rises to the water's surface (888) at 4630; the bank's floor
* goes on up from 888 to the mound and back down to its old level (866).
* Room 19 is only as tall as the water, so at its right end it narrows to
* nothing and the fish stay in. At its left end the floor rises steeply
* (941 to 888 over 22 px), too steep to walk: a norn walking west in the
* water used to reach the wall at x 4358, where its foot counted as in the
* rock column beyond (room 20, its doorway to the water solid), and it could
* not walk back out (regression batch reg4). Doorways: water to bank open; air over the
* pond to the bank stays solid (no walking out onto the water), the rest
* as they were.
